# Byte-exact checkout.
#
# This project's central claim is byte-level determinism: the same seed must
# produce the same pixels, verified by SHA-256. That claim is about image output,
# not source text, so line-ending conversion would not by itself break it.
#
# It is still wrong here. tools/verify_determinism.py digests generated images,
# and CI compares those digests across platforms. Normalising line endings makes
# the same commit produce different working trees on Windows and Linux, so "these
# two checkouts are the same project" stops being true -- and a reader comparing
# the two would be comparing files that differ for no reason the repository
# records.
#
# `* -text` marks every path as binary for git's purposes: no end-of-line
# conversion in either direction, on either platform.
* -text
